{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789495778,"nonce":"snu6mDYcE7giSlLq645l/FWhz10=","message":"Resolution: wontfix\n-------------------\n\n``b4.searchmask`` is being removed rather than restored. Searches are handled\nby liblore, and that is a deliberate architectural consolidation, not an\noversight in db4cd69.\n\n``searchmask`` bundled three orthogonal things into one printf template: the\norigin, the list path, and the query shape. liblore decomposed all three --\nthe origin into the node's origin list (with probing, failover and per-origin\n``[liblore \"\u003corigin\u003e\"]`` config), the list path into the node's base URL, and\nthe query shape into ``get_mbox_by_query(full_threads=...)``. No single URL\ntemplate can survive that split, which is why ``LoreNode.from_git_config()``\nhas nowhere to put it.\n\nIt is also the only mask in b4 that was purely about retrieval.\n``linkmask``, ``linktrailermask`` and ``thanks-commit-url-mask`` are\nrendering templates that printf into commit messages and outgoing mail and\nare unaffected; ``midmask`` survived because it has a rendering role\n(``ez.py:1703``, ``ez.py:2064``) in addition to seeding the node.\n\nHonouring a caller-supplied search URL again would be a downgrade, not a fix.\n``_rewrite_url()`` (``liblore/src/liblore/node.py:622-624``) rotates origins\nby swapping a prefix of a URL liblore composed itself, and ``_cache_key()``\n(``node.py:858-861``) produces mirror-shared cache keys for the same reason.\nA hand-built URL template participates in neither, so restoring the setting\nwould opt searches out of failover, probe reordering and mirror-shared\ncaching.\n\nGoing forward ``b4.midmask`` is the only way to name the public-inbox host,\nand liblore fallbacks are the multi-host mechanism.\n\nWhat remains actionable\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n- The setting is dropped from ``DEFAULT_CONFIG`` and documented as superseded\n  (not merely \"ignored\"), with a runtime warning when a user still has it\n  set. Handled by the list series that prompted this report.\n- Carrying failover configuration in ``.b4-config`` so projects can ship\n  mirror lists is tracked as a v0.17 item in ``plan.otl``. liblore's\n  fallbacks are origin-only today; the subpath generalisation is drafted in\n  ``liblore/.git/rfc-subpath-fallback.md``.\n\nNote on framing: the earlier statement in this report that the maintainer\nreply identified the setting as a regression rather than an intended\ndeprecation overstates it. The reply asked whether the removal was deliberate\nor an oversight; this resolution is the answer.","files":null}]}